      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Union business",
          "heading": "Bill Sweeney confirms WRU's bid to put Welsh clubs into the PREM",
          "body": "The RFU has received a formal request from the Welsh Rugby Union to bring Welsh clubs into the Gallagher PREM. Chief executive Bill Sweeney told BBC Radio Four the request had been put in writing, that the RFU would go back with questions, and that its focus remains on expanding the English game. The United Rugby Championship has meanwhile threatened the WRU, a shareholder, with legal action over plans to leave the competition."
        },
        {
